    <briefdescription>
<para>This node is the base class for sequential/in-order min/max selections. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Note that their fundamental difference from <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_s_c_e_v_min_max_expr" kindref="compound">SCEVMinMaxExpr</ref>&apos;s is that they are early-returning upon reaching saturation point. I.e. given <computeroutput>0 umin_seq poison</computeroutput>, the result will be <computeroutput>0</computeroutput>, while the result of <computeroutput>0 umin poison</computeroutput> is <computeroutput>poison</computeroutput>. When returning early, later expressions are not executed, so <computeroutput>0 umin_seq (x u/ 0)</computeroutput> does not result in undefined behavior. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
